iconic 0.9.3.1 (2026-07-23)
===========================

## Bug fixes

* Fixed crash in `infer_confounding()`, `iconic_sensitivity()`, and
  `iconic_prospect()` when the mediator instrument (Gm) is a panel
  (one F-statistic per gene). The diagnosis object stores `F_Gm` as a
  vector, but scalar comparisons (`is.na(F_Gm) || F_Gm < 10`,
  `F_gm >= 100`) and `sprintf("%.1f", F_Gm)` assumed a scalar. All
  three sites now collapse to `F_Gm_median` when `length(F_Gm) > 1`.
  The same fix is applied to `F_G` for symmetry.

  Affected files: `R/infer_confounding.R`, `R/model_sensitivity.R`,
  `R/prospect.R`.


iconic 0.9.3 (2026-07-22)
=========================

## New features

* Added `se_method = "composite"` option to `iconic_estimate()` and
  `analyze_mediation_robust()`, implementing the closed-form JT-comp
  composite null hypothesis test of Huang (2019) for the natural indirect
  effect (NIE) p-value. The composite test accounts for the three-case
  structure of H0: alpha_M * beta_M = 0 and provides higher power than
  the Sobel/delta test when signals are sparse. The test statistic is
  p_comp = F(ab/sqrt(Var(a))) + F(ab/sqrt(Var(b))) - F(ab), where F is
  the CDF of the standard normal product distribution and Var(a)/Var(b)
  are estimated per estimator across all tests sharing that estimator
  (i.e., across mediators and outcome features within each method),
  clamped to [1, 1.5]. Only the NIE p-value changes; all point estimates,
  standard errors, and the NDE p-value are unchanged. The output
  additionally includes `var_a` and `var_b` columns for transparency.
  Exported function: `composite_p_value()`.

* Added `alpha_M`, `alpha_se`, `beta_M`, `beta_M_se` columns to the
  return value of all eight mediation estimators, enabling the composite
  test and providing users with the raw stage-1 and stage-2 regression
  coefficients and standard errors.

## Bug fixes

* Fixed composite test grouping in `.apply_composite_pvalues()`: variance
  is now estimated per method across all tests (mediators and outcome
  features) sharing that estimator, rather than per (method, mediator)
  group. The previous grouping gave one test per group when the outcome
  was scalar (the real case study design), falling back to Var = 1 and
  making the composite test a no-op. The method-only grouping correctly
  estimates Var(a) from the variation in stage-1 regressions M_m ~ Z
  across mediators.

* Fixed bootstrap p-value computation in `.with_se()`: when
  `se_method = "bootstrap"`, the NDE and NIE p-values are now recomputed
  as two-sided Wald tests using the bootstrap standard errors
  (2 * pnorm(-abs(estimate / bootstrap_se))), rather than retaining the
  delta-method p-values. This ensures the reported p-values are
  consistent with the reported bootstrap confidence intervals.

* Fixed a duplicate field in the return list of `fit_iv2sls_mediation2()`
  where `alpha_M`, `alpha_se`, `beta_M`, `beta_M_se` were listed twice.

* Fixed missing `alpha_M`, `alpha_se`, `beta_M`, `beta_M_se` fields in
  the return list of `fit_pgc_mediation2()`, which caused
  `data.frame()` errors in downstream `row()` construction.

## Documentation

* Updated vignette (`iconic-walkthrough.Rmd`) with a new "Standard errors
  and p-values (`se_method`)" section comparing the three inference
  options (delta, bootstrap, composite), including the JT-comp formula,
  what changes in the output, and known limitations.

* Updated README with a `se_method` comparison table and composite null
  explanation.

* Updated test suite: added `test-v0.9.3-composite.R` with 25 tests
  covering `.np_cdf()`, `composite_p_value()`, `.apply_composite_pvalues()`,
  end-to-end integration via both `analyze_mediation_robust()` and
  `iconic_estimate()`, and the real case study design (scalar outcome,
  multiple mediators). Fixed stale `expect_named()` calls in
  `test-mediation.R` and `test-estimators.R`.


iconic 0.9.2 (2026-07-21)
=========================

* GAN-based generative texture model for synthetic data construction.
* Gaussian copula model for mediator panel feature-level joint distribution.
* `infer_confounding()` for data-driven confounding parameter estimation.
* `iconic_prospect()` for prospective analysis without instruments/NCs.
* `iconic_diagnose()` with instrument-strength, NC validity, and
  path-completeness assessment.
* Eight mediation estimators (UNADJ, DIRECT, COCA, IV2SLS, PGC, IV2SLS2,
  PGC2, PGC2Gm) with NDE/NIE decomposition.
* `iconic_sensitivity()` degradation surface over instrument exogeneity
  violations.
* `iconic_recommend()` estimator ranking by identification tier and
  robustness.
* Publication figure plotting functions (ggplot2 + patchwork).
* Multi-core parallelization via `n_cores` argument.


iconic 0.9.0 (2026-07-15)
=========================

* Initial public release.
